# UI Component Standards

Read `docs/03-COMPONENT_GUIDELINES.md`.

## General
- Inspect existing components before creating new ones.
- Use shadcn/ui and Radix primitives where appropriate.
- Keep component APIs small and typed.
- Avoid premature abstraction and nested wrappers.
- Ensure keyboard accessibility and visible focus.

## Buttons
- Restrained variants: default, secondary, outline, ghost, destructive, link.
- One dominant primary action per context where possible.
- Icon-only buttons need accessible names.
- Include loading and disabled states.

## Inputs
- Consistent height, label, help text, focus and error states.
- Placeholder never replaces a label.
- Associate labels and controls semantically.

## Tables
- Follow the installed TanStack Table version.
- Numeric columns right-aligned and tabular.
- Text columns left-aligned.
- Compact but readable rows.
- Subtle separators; avoid vertical grid clutter.
- Real sorting/filtering/pagination state only.
- Include loading, empty, error and permission states.
- Do not badge every cell.

## Forms
- React Hook Form + Zod when appropriate.
- Keep validation close to fields.
- Preserve user input after recoverable errors.
- Prevent accidental duplicate submissions.

## Dialogs
- Use accessible primitives.
- Clear title and action hierarchy.
- Confirm destructive actions.
- Do not cram long workflows into small dialogs.

## Icons
- Lucide React.
- Usually 16px; consistent stroke.
- Icons should improve recognition, not decorate.
